      "answerSummary": "The values are$\\ln100\\approx4.61$and$\\ln1000\\approx6.91$. The values are$0.990$and$0.999$. The antiderivative is$-1/(2x^2)$. The definite integral is$1/2-1/(2n^2)=(n^2-1)/(2n^2)$. $1/(2n^2)\\to0$as$n\\to\\infty$. The improper integral converges to$1/2$. The antiderivative is$2\\sqrt{x}$. The value is$2\\sqrt n-2$. $2\\sqrt n-2\\to+\\infty$, so the integral diverges. The antiderivative is$-x^{-p}/p$. The definite integral is$(1-n^{-p})/p$. The value is$1/p$. For$p<0$, $(1-n^{-p})/p\\to+\\infty$, so it diverges. $p=2024$, so the result is$1/2024$. $dy/dx=1/(x\\ln x)$. The result is$\\ln(\\ln n)-\\ln(\\ln2)$. $\\ln(\\ln n)\\to+\\infty$, so the integral diverges. The integral becomes$\\int u^{-p-1}du=-u^{-p}/p+C$. The result is$-1/[p(\\ln x)^p]+C$. $1/[p(\\ln2)^p]-1/[p(\\ln n)^p]$. The term$(\\ln n)^{-p}$tends to zero, giving$1/[p(\\ln2)^p]$. The integral diverges to$+\\infty$. $-e^{-px}/p+C$. $(1-e^{-pn})/p$. $e^{-pn}\\to0$and the integral equals$1/p$.",
