      "stem": "A fair six-sided die has its faces labelled $1,2,3,5,6,m$, where the mean of the six labels is $3.5$. In the first game, players $P_1$ and $P_2$ take turns, starting with $P_1$. A player wins immediately on rolling the face labelled $m$; otherwise the next player rolls. All throws are independent. Unless a different game is specified, play continues until someone wins.",
